From dea1d11e2a0866a58db2d3c60e81772a04a402a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:29:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] locale: Take setlocale and newlocale's "" locale from
 the environment

A locale name of "" means the locale the environment names: LC_ALL,
then the category's LC_* variable, then LANG, ignoring empty values
(XBD 8.2). setlocale and newlocale ignored the environment and always
used the default. setlocale(LC_ALL, "") now checks every category's
value before changing anything and fails if any names a locale that
doesn't exist; newlocale fails with ENOENT.
---
 doc/build.md                 |  5 ++-
 libc/locale/CMakeLists.txt   |  1 +
 libc/locale/locale_env.c     | 73 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libc/locale/locale_private.h |  2 +
 libc/locale/meson.build      |  1 +
 libc/locale/newlocale.c      | 30 ++++++++++++---
 libc/locale/setlocale.c      | 19 +++++++++-
 7 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libc/locale/locale_env.c

diff --git a/doc/build.md b/doc/build.md
index 8cfe756de2..6afd3d74ea 100644
--- a/doc/build.md
+++ b/doc/build.md
@@ -127,7 +127,10 @@ These options control how much internationalization support is included
 in the library. Picolibc supports locale names of the form '<locale>' or
 '<locale>.<charset>'; e.g. POSIX or C.UTF-8. When no charset is
 specified, picolibc selects ASCII when multi-byte support is disabled
-or locale is C. Otherwise, picolibc selects UTF-8.
+or locale is C. Otherwise, picolibc selects UTF-8. A name of "" takes
+the locale from the LC_ALL, LC_* and LANG environment variables, as
+POSIX describes; setlocale and newlocale fail when that names a
+charset the library doesn't have.
 
 Picolibc supports the same charsets for locales and iconv.
 
